**A computer-implemented method for tone-reservation optimization, comprising:**

1. selecting a plurality of carrier indices to form an initial tone-reservation index set;

2. generating a kernel signal based on the selected carrier indices;

3. preliminarily determining a plurality of candidate carrier indices and reordering the candidate carrier indices according to a predetermined ordering criterion;

4. for each candidate carrier index, testing replacement of at least one carrier index in the initial tone-reservation index set with the candidate carrier index;

5. determining, for each resulting tone-reservation index set, an average comparison metric based on a signal generated using the resulting tone-reservation index set; and

6. selecting, as an optimized tone-reservation index set, the resulting tone-reservation index set having a minimum average comparison metric.
